  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe introduce a multi-resolution optimization with structured initializer and repair mechanism designed to escape local optima. The core idea is to:\n1. Start with a symmetric, band-pass filtered initializer (derived from the triangular parent) to inject structured variation\n2. Use repair functions that clip and rescale to maintain feasibility\n3. Combine global exploration with directed local search\n4. Run in phases: coarse optimization at 140-point resolution \u2192 mirroring to 280 points \u2192 fine tuning\n\nThe main bottleneck is the computation's expense at higher resolutions. This approach aims to find a function that's both spectrally thin and sparsely correlated with its shifts.\n\nMathematical specifications:\nVariables: h_vec \u2208 [0,1]^140 (first half), then mirrored to form 280-point function\nObjective: C5 = (2/280) * max_k |(h_full \u22c6 (1-h_full))[k]| (full cross-correlation)\nConstraints:\n  \u2211h_vec[i] = 70 exactly (because dx=2/280, so integral(h)=1 requires sum(h)=70)\n  0 \u2264 h_vec[i] \u2264 1 for all i\nRepresentation: Use grid spacing dx=2/280, support [0,2] via mirrored hard endpoint\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Validate input resolution (default=280)\n2. If 'initial_h_values' available, use it directly\n3. Generate initializer: Apply band-pass filter to triangular parent\n   - Basis: w = initial_triangular_parent.copy()\n   - Filter: Smooth with multiple Gaussian kernels to remove high/low-frequency components\n4. Phase 1: Optimizer setup\n   - Method: SLSQP\n   - Use parent if available (priority seed 0)\n   - Else: Create 4 initial points via random walk + repair\n5. Phase 2: Constraint repair\n   - Clip outside [0,1] then scale to meet integral constraint\n   - Handling: Linear interpolation + gradient projection\n6. Phase 3: Multi-resolution loop\n   - Coarse (140 points): Run 50 steps\n   - Mirror to 280 points\n   - Fine (full 280): Run 200 steps\n   - Local repair at every step\n7. Phase 4: Local refinement (optional)\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Initializer generation: \n  - F = 0.32 (trimming factor)\n  - \u03c3_smooth = [0.01, 0.05] (Gaussian kernel standard deviations)\n  - Apply to initial_triangular_parent\n- Optimization:\n  - Max iterations: 250 (40+210)\n  - ftol=1e-6 (function tolerance)\n  - Time budget: Monitor per-evaluation cost\n- Post-processing:\n  - Merging on diversity below 0.001\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n- Primary cost: correlation+(function value) ~ O(n^2)\n- Cache evaluations to avoid recomputation\n- Use fallback initial candidate if timeout\n- Graceful degradation: Exit early with best candidate\n\nValidation and return contract:\n1. Check integral: sum(h_values)*dx \u2248 1.0 (tolerance=1e-4)\n2. Verify bounds: all(h_values \u2208 [0,1])\n3. Re-evaluate final candidate with task's correlation\n4. Return tuple: (h_values, final_c5, n_points=280)\n5. Score comparisons use exact correlation via provided eval",
